title Loops: a loop recorded on Play and layered, the Looper tab's tools, loops launched from Arrange
covers looper, rec-arm, loop-tracks, looper-deck, loop-cell
# The looper records what the pads play (Input: Pads), so it needs no
# cable. On the MPC this window also shows what recording and playing
# loops cost (the report's "looper" rows).
wait 1
mark record
tap play-loop arm Arm
expect rec: the loop armed
button REC
expect looper: Record: armed, the first pass starts on the next bar line
button PLAY
pad 1 120 0.3
wait 1.7
button REC
expect looper: Record during the first pass: it ends on the next bar line
wait 2
expect looper: loop of 2 bars
expect time: Loop 1 on Loops A, row 1, playing
mark overdub
button OVERDUB
expect looper: overdub on (layer 2)
pad 3 100
pad 3 100
wait 2
button OVERDUB
expect looper: overdub off
wait 1
mark looper-tab
tap header tab Looper
tap leditor speed Speed 2×
expect looper: speed 2×: an octave up, half the bars
wait 2
tap leditor speed Speed 1×
tap leditor reverse Reverse
wait 2
tap leditor reverse Reverse on
expect looper: edit Reverse
tap ldeck loop-mute Loop 1 speaker
expect looper: loop 1 muted
wait 2
tap ldeck loop-mute Loop 1 speaker
expect looper: loop 1 unmuted
# A second loop from its ring: it records two bars from the next bar line.
tap ldeck ring Loop 2 ring: record
pad 5 100
wait 4
tap ldeck ring Loop 2 ring: close and play
wait 2
expect time: Loop 2 on Loops B, row 1, playing
button-down SHIFT
button REC
button-up SHIFT
expect looper: Capture: on the bar line coming, the last 2 bars become Loop 3
wait 1
mark arrange
tap header tab Arrange
tap clips pager Tracks after
tap clips slot Loops A slot 1
wait 4
expect looper: loop 1 off from bar
tap clips stop-all Stop all
expect time: stop all
wait 4
tap clips scene Scene 1
expect time: scene 1
wait 4
expect looper: loop 3 on from bar
button STOP
button STOP
expect STOP: all sounds stopped
